SamenvattingFor our client in Oud-Beijerland, we are looking for experienced machine operators. This is a full-time position in potato production. It is an ideal opportunity for people who want to work in a modern production facility and are looking for stable employment.Over de functieAs a machine operator at our production facility, you will help ensure that the potatoes reach our customers in perfect condition and in the correct portions. You will work together with a team that is responsible for maintaining quality at every stage of the production process.
Your responsibilities will include:
Operating and monitoring production machinery;
Checking the quality of the products produced;
Maintaining order, cleanliness and safety at the workplace;
Working together with the production team and technical department;
Reporting on the progress of the work according to the applicable procedures.

You will work in a 2-shift system. The working hours are:
06:00/07:00 - 15:00/16:00 or 15:00/16:00 - 22:00/23:00
Over het bedrijfPotatoNext aims to be a reliable partner throughout the entire potato supply chain. Their goal is to take away the worries of growers and buyers. Through continuous innovation and smart, efficient production, PotatoNext is working on a future-proof product that provides added value in many areas.
PotatoNext currently operates at the locations of the former companies Nedato and Leo de Kock, respectively in Oud-Beijerland and Purmerend. In the near future, the large facility in Oud-Beijerland will become the heart of our dynamic organization.
Wat wij vragenYou have your own accommodation and transportation to work;
You speak English or Dutch;
You have experience as a machine operator;
You are available to work in a 2-shift system.

Wat wij biedenStarting salary of €2,611 gross per month up to €2,868 gross per month;
Monday to Friday: 25% allowance between 19:00 and 00:00 / 40% between 00:00 and 06:00;
Saturday: 25% between 15:00 and 23:00 / 40% be

- Packing and repacking products into cardboard export boxes;
- Preparing creams in a 400-liter mixing tank according to established formulas;
- Operating filling machines for tubes, wound care products, and FFP2 face masks;
- Replenishing raw materials and production supplies;
- Accurately completing production and quality documentation;
- Identifying and resolving minor technical issues;
- Setting up and changing over production lines;
- Supporting warehouse operations when needed;
- Working in accordance with CE, FDA, and cleanroom guidelines;
- Contributing ideas for process improvements and preventing recurring technical issues.

The company places a strong emphasis on independence. You will be trained to operate multiple machines and production stations independently as part of your development within the organization.

- Holds at least a VAPRO A diploma or an equivalent qualification;
- Speaks and writes either Dutch or English;
- Has technical insight and can analyze and solve equipment malfunctions;
- Works accurately, takes responsibility, and can work independently;
- Feels comfortable in an environment where quality standards and procedures are important;
- Brings discipline, energy, and a positive attitude to work.

Would you like to contribute to flawless mail delivery and are you looking for a flexible part-time job? Become a mail preparer at our client in Assen! In this role, you will be responsible for ensuring that mail is correctly sorted and prepared for dispatch.

As a mail preparer in Assen, you are responsible for accurately sorting incoming mail. You will check addresses and shipping details and use various mail processing machines to handle the mail efficiently. The job requires precision and good physical condition, as you will be working primarily on your feet. You should also be open to working overtime to assist your colleagues during backlogs or busy periods.

What we ask for:

- No minimum educational requirements;
- Precision and attention to detail;
- Enthusiastic and motivated attitude;
- You speak either Dutch or English;
- Availability for 3 days, between Monday to Thursday.
